# Guardrails ({{project_name}})

<!-- Owned by the project; /sync never touches it. Only the "Signs" section is sent to the local worker with every
     request, so keep it short (20 signs at most). This file is advice: a rule that must never be broken belongs in
     a gate or in [scope] protected of .harness/harness.toml, and is only pointed to here. -->

## Enforced (not advice)
- Protected and generated paths: `[scope] protected` in `.harness/harness.toml`. The worker script rejects edits to them.
- Files outside a task's "Files in scope": rejected by the scope guard.
- Fast and full gates: `[gates]` in `.harness/harness.toml`. A failing gate sends the task back to the worker.
- Tools the worker may run: derived from the gate commands; the rest of the permissions are in `.claude/settings.json`.

